        "id": 1337669
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-01-03T14:16:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This change is ready for review.\n\nDoesn\u0027t need a stub. Static linking liblog is enough, as toolbox uses only the stdio logger and kmsg logger. It never uses logd.\n\nI\u0027ve added a build time flag to ensure it only ever tried to use the kernel logger when executed from the ramdisk. However if this is executed before the /dev/kmsg node is created, then the logs would probably be lost, I think?\nI think this *should* be fine probably, as libmodprobe usually doesn\u0027t generate a lot of logs. Even if some kernel module failed to load and the error log message is dropped, this should leave the system in a broken enough state that other system components can report the module failure in some other way.",
      "parentUuid": "c84c6be3_09ed765e",
      "revId": "0950a59dd6e73d6bdbd43c6966d10e40896e1841",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
